---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
import CtaBand from "../components/CtaBand.astro";
import { SITE } from "../config";
---

<Base
  title="About Kirpik"
  description="Kirpik is built by INFOWISE LIMITED, the developer of Tilkie image protection, to give Shopify merchants a way to prove ownership of their own text."
>
  <PageHero
    title="About Kirpik"
    lead="Kirpik is built by INFOWISE LIMITED for Shopify merchants who write their own product descriptions, blog articles and pages."
  />

  <section class="section" style="padding-top:0">
    <div class="container narrow prose">
      <h2>Why we built it</h2>
      <p>
        Good product writing takes real work. Copying it takes none: every
        Shopify store publishes its product text in feeds designed for
        software to read. The apps sold as the answer mostly disable
        right-click, which inconveniences customers and does nothing to stop
        copying.
      </p>
      <p>
        We took a different position: copying cannot be prevented, so anything
        copied should be traceable. Kirpik embeds an invisible watermark in
        your product descriptions, blog articles and pages without modifying
        your content. When your text appears on another site, Kirpik detects
        the watermark on any page you check, and you can issue a Proof of
        Ownership Certificate.
      </p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        Kirpik is developed by {SITE.developer}, a small team that builds
        practical software for merchants. We hold this site to the same
        standard as the product: no invented statistics and no claims Kirpik
        cannot back up. Where Kirpik has limits, we say so plainly.
      </p>

      <h2>Kirpik and Tilkie</h2>
      <p>
        <a href="https://tilkie.app" rel="noopener">Tilkie</a>, also developed
        by {SITE.developer}, does for product images what Kirpik does for
        text: an invisible watermark, detection and a Proof of Ownership
        Certificate. The two apps are designed to run side by side.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions and bug reports go to
        <a href="mailto:support@kirpik.app">support@kirpik.app</a>. The
        <a href="/support/">Support page</a> lists the other ways to reach us.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand />
</Base>
